{"title": "US Issues Advisory for Citizens in Middle East Amid Tensions", "summary": "The US government has issued an advisory for its citizens currently in the Middle East due to rising tensions. The advisory urges Americans to remain vigilant and consider departing the region. The advisory was issued by the US Department of State, which stated that 'the situation is fluid' and that 'American citizens are advised to be aware of their surroundings.' The advisory applies to several countries in the Middle East, including Saudi Arabia, Yemen, and Iraq. No specific threats were mentioned, but the advisory emphasizes the need for caution. The move comes amid a surge in tensions between the US and Iran, as well as other regional players.", "summary_points": ["The US government has issued an advisory for its citizens currently in the Middle East."], "title_hi": "", "summary_hi": "", "summary_points_hi": [], "framing": {}, "framing_hi": {}, "topic": "Society", "region": "World", "image_url": "https://c.ndtvimg.com/2026-08/4nnkt1kg_iran_625x300_02_August_26.jpeg?im=FitAndFill,algorithm=dnn,width=1280,height=720", "sources": [{"source": "NDTV", "owner": "NDTV", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-iran-war-middle-east-travel-advisory-after-donald-trumps-hit-them-hard-threat-us-tells-citizens-to-leave-middle-east-middle-east-conflict-11854544", "headline": "\"Prepare To Depart\": US' Advisory For Its Citizens In Mideast Amid Tensions"}, {"source": "The New Indian Express", "owner": "The New Indian Express", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "US embassies urge American citizens to 'consider departing' Middle East"}, {"source": "Mathrubhumi English", "owner": "Mathrubhumi English", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "US asks Americans across Middle East to stay ready to leave as Iran tensions deepen"}, {"source": "France 24", "owner": "Fra